From: Rob Vogelaar <revogelaar@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] agent: re-send M1 to recover a lost WSC M2

On a multi-radio extender all radios run WSC near-simultaneously (M1s go out within tens
of ms). The controller answers each with exactly one M2 and never retransmits, so if one
radio's M2 is lost or arrives while that radio is momentarily not in wsc_m2_pending, it is
dropped for good: analyze_m2ctrl_configuration is never called for that radio, its Private
VAP subdoc is never pushed to OneWifi, OneWifi never applies a Vap_<band> doc for it, and
wifi_hal_createVAP is never invoked -- so that radio's fronthaul VAP never beacons and the
device onboards with a straggler radio down (observed: 3x wsc m1 send success but only 2x
received wsc_m2 / vap create radio_index). It is random which radio loses; nothing
self-heals it.

Recover at the agent: while a radio waits in wsc_m2_pending, re-send its M1 a bounded
number of times to solicit a fresh M2. The controller already handles a duplicate M1 by
re-issuing M2 (Removing previous em_config command for radio ...), and this touches nothing
but the WSC handshake (no VAP teardown, no shared timers). Self-clearing once M2 is handled.
---
 inc/em_configuration.h             |  8 ++++
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 42 +++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/inc/em_configuration.h b/inc/em_configuration.h
--- a/inc/em_configuration.h
+++ b/inc/em_configuration.h
@@ -1597,6 +1597,14 @@ private:
     unsigned char m_m2_encrypted_settings[em_haul_type_max][MAX_EM_BUFF_SZ];
     unsigned int m_m2_encrypted_settings_len[em_haul_type_max];
 
+    // WSC M2-loss recovery (agent): a radio's M2 can be lost when several radios do
+    // WSC near-simultaneously; the controller sends M2 only once, so the radio is
+    // stranded. These count 1s ticks spent waiting in wsc_m2_pending and bound the
+    // number of M1 re-sends used to solicit a fresh M2. Reset each time a fresh M1 is
+    // sent (handle_autoconfig_resp).
+    unsigned int m_wsc_m2_wait_ticks = 0;
+    unsigned int m_wsc_m1_resends = 0;
+
 public:
 
 	bool send_autoconf_search_ext_chirp(em_dpp_chirp_value_t *chirp, size_t hash_len);
diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -5677,8 +5689,11 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_autoconfig_resp(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int
     }
     em_printfout("autoconfig wsc m1 send success, len:%d", sz);
     set_state(em_state_agent_wsc_m2_pending);
+    // Fresh M1 sent -- re-arm the M2-loss recovery window for this radio.
+    m_wsc_m2_wait_ticks = 0;
+    m_wsc_m1_resends = 0;
 
-    return 0;   
+    return 0;
 }
 
 int em_configuration_t::handle_autoconfig_search(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int len)
@@ -6024,9 +6075,45 @@ void em_configuration_t::handle_state_wsc_m1_pending()
     assert(get_service_type() == em_service_type_ctrl);
 }
 
+// WSC M2-loss recovery tunables (agent). process_agent_state ticks ~1s while the
+// dev_init/cfg_renew orch is in progress, so RESEND_TICKS is ~seconds between M1
+// re-sends and MAX_RESENDS bounds them within the orch's time-to-live.
+#define EM_AGENT_M2_RESEND_TICKS 3
+#define EM_AGENT_M2_MAX_RESENDS  4
+
 void em_configuration_t::handle_state_wsc_m2_pending()
 {
     assert(get_service_type() == em_service_type_agent);
+
+    // A radio's M2 can be lost/dropped when several radios run WSC near-simultaneously
+    // -- the controller sends each M2 only once, so a lost M2 strands the radio in
+    // wsc_m2_pending forever: its VAP subdoc is never pushed and its fronthaul VAP is
+    // never created (createVAP is never called for it). Re-send M1 a bounded number of
+    // times to solicit a fresh M2; the controller re-issues M2 on a duplicate M1
+    // ("Removing previous em_config command for radio ..."). Self-clearing: once the
+    // M2 is handled the radio leaves wsc_m2_pending and this stops firing.
+    if (++m_wsc_m2_wait_ticks < EM_AGENT_M2_RESEND_TICKS) {
+        return;
+    }
+    m_wsc_m2_wait_ticks = 0;
+    if (m_wsc_m1_resends >= EM_AGENT_M2_MAX_RESENDS) {
+        return;
+    }
+
+    unsigned char msg[MAX_EM_BUFF_SZ];
+    int msg_len = create_autoconfig_wsc_m1_msg(msg, get_peer_mac());
+    if (msg_len < 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    if (send_frame(msg, static_cast<unsigned int>(msg_len)) < 0) {
+        em_printfout("radio %s wsc_m2_pending re-send M1 failed, errno:%d",
+            util::mac_to_string(get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str(), errno);
+        return;
+    }
+    m_wsc_m1_resends++;
+    em_printfout("radio %s stuck in wsc_m2_pending -- re-sent M1 to solicit M2 (attempt %u/%d)",
+        util::mac_to_string(get_radio_interface_mac()).c_str(), m_wsc_m1_resends,
+        EM_AGENT_M2_MAX_RESENDS);
 }
 
 void em_configuration_t::fill_media_data(em_media_spec_data_t *spec, dm_bss_t *bss)
